-s
sudo systemctl status amazon-cloudwatch-agent

#Then comes EC2 #2

This is where the real benefit of SSM becomes clear.

We install the CloudWatch Agent on EC2 #2, but we don't need to create another configuration.

EC2 #2 simply does:

Fetch same configuration
        ↓
AmazonCloudWatch-linux
        ↓
Start CloudWatch Agent

So let's first get EC2 #1 running and verify its metrics/logs. Then we'll configure EC2 #2 using the exact same SSM parameter.

